| *A single‑stage PD on the pole is enough* | The pole dynamics are second‑order and the controller must also damp the cart motion; otherwise the cart drifts, the pole angle grows, and the controller saturates. |
| *Clipping the force at ±3 N is harmless* | It is the main cause of early failure – the controller asks for ≈ ‑5 N when θ≈0.2 rad, but the environment only gives ‑3 N, so the pole keeps accelerating. |

