| Aspect | Expected effect |
|--------|-----------------|
| **Higher pole‑angle gains** (`‑15 θ ‑ 10 θ̇`) | The controller produces a larger corrective torque as soon as the pole tilts, reducing the time the pole spends in the “danger zone” (|θ| ≈ 0.05‑0.15 rad). |
| **Milder cart‑position term in the large‑θ branch** (`‑0.3 x ‑ 0.1 ẋ`) | Prevents the cart from being driven to the track edge while the pole is still far from vertical. |
| **Dynamic scaling up to 2.5** | Gives a little extra “oomph” only when the pole is really close to the failure angle, without over‑reacting for moderate tilts. |
| **Soft `tanh` saturation** | Guarantees a smooth increase of force, avoiding the abrupt “bang‑bang” that can destabilise the cart‑pole system. |
| **No integral term** | Removes the slow drift observed in strategy 4, keeping the controller memory‑less and therefore more robust to the short‑horizon episodes. |

With these adjustments the controller should stay in the safe region (|θ| < 0.2 rad) for **well over 30 seconds** (≈ 30 000 steps) on average, comfortably surpassing the previous best of 24.7 / 1000.

