| **Squared boost term** | When the pole is clearly out of the small‑angle region the boost adds a *non‑linear* torque that grows quickly with the deviation, helping to “catch” the pole before the angular velocity becomes too large. |
| **Mild cart‑position feedback** (k_x, k_x_dot) | Keeps the cart from drifting to the edges while the pole is being corrected, which was a weakness of the best‑so‑far strategy. |
| **tanh soft‑saturation** | Guarantees a smooth control signal (good for the continuous‑force actuator) while still allowing the controller to saturate at the physical limit when necessary. |

