| **Linear interpolation between the modes** | Guarantees continuity of the control signal, eliminating the sudden jumps that caused the pole to overshoot in the earlier attempts. |
| **Extra boost for |θ| > 0.20 rad** | When the pole is already close to the failure limit we need a stronger corrective torque; the boost factor grows with the angle, giving the controller enough authority to pull the pole back before the episode ends. |
| **Separate gain sets (kx/kẋ vs kθ/kθ̇)** | Allows us to *de‑emphasise* cart‑position when the pole is far from vertical, preventing the tug‑of‑war between “centre the cart” and “stop the fall”. |
