       ≈ 0.096 -0.136 + 22.2 -10.9  ≈ 11.26
```

`u_smooth = 3 * tanh(11.26/3) ≈ 3.0` → **max rightward force**.  
The pole is leaning left (θ = ‑1.85 rad ≈ ‑106°) – the controller pushes hard to the right, exactly what we need to swing the pole back toward vertical. The previous PD (Kθ≈‑1) would have produced only ~‑2 N, far too weak.

