| **Cart‑PD always present** | Removing the cart term when the pole is far from vertical caused the cart to drift and the pole to fall. | `Kx` and `Kx_d` never go to zero; they simply become smaller as the angle term dominates. |
| **Gravity feed‑forward** | Helps the angle controller cancel the constant torque of gravity, especially near the limits. | `u_grav = -0.5·sin(theta)` is added to the raw command for every step. |
| **Tiny safety margin (0.05 N)** | Larger margins (0.12 N) reduced usable authority and shortened episodes. | The margin is now only 0.05 N, enough to avoid numerical overflow while preserving most of the control range. |
| **Clipping only at the very end** | Early clipping distorted the PD law and produced “jumps”. | The PD law works on the unrestricted `u_raw`; we clip only after the margin step. |

