| **Tilt‑dependent scaling (max ≈ 3.5)** | Provides enough torque when the pole is far from vertical while keeping the gain modest near the upright position (avoids overshoot). |
| **Smooth tanh saturation** | Removes the discontinuity at ±3 N, allowing the controller to “lean into” the limit rather than hitting it abruptly and then fighting the opposite direction. |
| **Gain values** | Slightly reduced from the original 30/8 pair (28/7.5) to lower the aggressiveness; cart gains (1.2/0.25) are enough to keep the cart centred without causing large accelerations. |

