**Bottom line:** The “scaled‑angle” rule set is the clear winner among the three candidates. By tightening the cart‑controller, sharpening the angle gains, and smoothly scaling the angle torque as the pole tilts, we obtain a more decisive corrective action while still respecting the force limits. Implement the pseudocode above and you should see a noticeable jump in episode length. Good luck!
