## Updated strategy (Policy 4)

Below is a compact pseudo‑code that combines the best ideas of the previous attempts and adds a light cart‑centering term for the whole operating range.

```
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# 0. Safety guard
IF NOT ( isFinite(x) AND isFinite(x_dot) AND
         isFinite(theta) AND isFinite(theta_dot) ) THEN
    force ← 0.0
    RETURN force
END IF

# 1. Hard emergency when the pole is already out of the safe band
IF abs(theta) ≥ 0.18 THEN
    # push with maximum opposite force
    force ← clamp( -sign(theta) * 3.0 , -3.0 , 3.0 )
    RETURN force
END IF

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Parameter definitions (tuned by hand, but simple)
Kx          ← 0.4          # cart‑position gain (small)
Kx_dot      ← 0.6          # cart‑velocity gain (small)

Kθ_base     ← 20.0         # base angle‑gain when |θ| = 0.02
Kθ_dot_base ← 5.0          # base angular‑velocity gain

Kθ_max      ← 70.0         # max angle‑gain when |θ| → 0.18
Kθ_dot_max  ← 13.0         # max angular‑velocity gain

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Decide which regime we are in
IF abs(theta) ≤ 0.02 THEN
    # --------------------------------------------------------------
    #   Very small angle → only centre the cart
    u_angle ← 0.0
    u_cart  ← -( Kx * x + Kx_dot * x_dot )
ELSE
    # --------------------------------------------------------------
    #   Moderate tilt → angle control + a *very* light cart term
    #   Interpolate gains linearly between the “small‑angle” and
    #   “near‑failure” values.
    z ← (abs(theta) - 0.02) / (0.18 - 0.02)      # 0 … 1

    Kθ       ← Kθ_base       + z * (Kθ_max       - Kθ_base)
    Kθ_dot   ← Kθ_dot_base   + z * (Kθ_dot_max   - Kθ_dot_base)

    # Angle‑torque (dominant term)
    u_angle ← -( Kθ * theta + Kθ_dot * theta_dot )

    # Light cart‑centering (helps keep the cart from drifting)
    u_cart  ← -( 0.2 * Kx * x + 0.2 * Kx_dot * x_dot )
END IF

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Combine the two torques, saturate and apply a dead‑zone
raw_force ← u_angle + u_cart
force     ← clamp( raw_force , -3.0 , 3.0 )

# Tiny dead‑zone to avoid jitter when the controller output is ≈0
IF abs(force) < 0.001 THEN force ← 0.0 END IF

RETURN force
```

