* **Limit the magnitude of the scaling** so that the force never exceeds the physical bound (±3 N) and never becomes too aggressive.  
* **Add a small “position‑only” bias** when the pole is almost upright to keep the cart near the centre of the track (otherwise the cart drifts).  

### 3. Updated rule‑set (pseudo‑code)

```text
# -------------------------------------------------
# Helper
clamp(v, lo, hi) = max(lo, min(hi, v))
sign(v)          =  1 if v>0 else -1 if v<0 else 0
# -------------------------------------------------
# Gains (tuned by hand – they are close to the optimal LQR for the
# classic cart‑pole with m_cart=1 kg, m_pole=0.1 kg, l=0.5 m)
Kx        = 0.55
Kx_dot    = 0.85
Ktheta    = 13.0
Ktheta_dot= 3.5

# Safety thresholds
THETA_MAX   = 0.20          # failure angle (rad)
THETA_SAFE  = 0.18          # start safety‑push
THETA_SMALL = 0.02          # start using full‑state LQR
THETA_MED   = 0.12          # centre of the “medium” band

# Main controller
IF NOT (isFinite(x) AND isFinite(x_dot) AND isFinite(theta) AND isFinite(theta_dot))
    force ← 0.0

ELSE IF abs(theta) ≥ THETA_SAFE
    # Very large tilt → maximal corrective push
    force ← clamp( -sign(theta) * 3.0 , -3.0 , 3.0 )

ELSE
    # -------------------------------------------------
    # 1) Compute the pure‑angle command (used everywhere)
    u_angle ← -( Ktheta * theta + Ktheta_dot * theta_dot )

    # 2) Compute the full‑state LQR command (used near vertical)
    u_full  ← -( Kx * x + Kx_dot * x_dot + Ktheta * theta + Ktheta_dot * theta_dot )

    # 3) Blend the two commands smoothly
    #    a) When |θ| ≤ THETA_SMALL → use full LQR
    #    b) When THETA_SMALL < |θ| < THETA_MED → linear blend
    #    c) When |θ| ≥ THETA_MED → use pure angle (but limited)
    IF abs(theta) ≤ THETA_SMALL
        raw ← u_full
    ELSE IF abs(theta) < THETA_MED
        # blend factor goes from 1 (full LQR) to 0 (pure angle)
        blend ← (THETA_MED - abs(theta)) / (THETA_MED - THETA_SMALL)   # 0 … 1
        raw   ← blend * u_full + (1‑blend) * u_angle
    ELSE
        # medium‑angle region – keep only the angle part
        raw ← u_angle
    END IF

    # 4) Optional tiny bias to keep the cart near the centre
    #    (only active when the pole is almost upright)
    IF abs(theta) ≤ 0.01
        bias ← -0.1 * x          # pull cart toward x = 0
        raw  ← raw + bias
    END IF

    # 5) Clamp to the actuator limits
    force ← clamp( raw , -3.0 , 3.0 )
END IF
