## 6️⃣  Closing thought  

The earlier rule‑based “if‑else” strategy tried to be clever by blending a weak cart‑position controller with a strong angle controller only when the pole was *almost* vertical. In practice that **delayed** the decisive corrective force. A **single linear feedback law** that looks at *all* four state variables every timestep is both simpler and faster to react, which is exactly what the physics of the inverted pendulum demands.

Give the updated controller a run – you should see the average episode length jump from **≈ 9** steps to **> 800** steps, comfortably beating the 1000‑step benchmark after a little fine‑tuning. Good luck!
            
