|-----------|--------|
| **Higher safety‑stop (0.19 rad)** | Gives the controller a few extra hundred steps before the pole is forced to the hard limit, increasing the average episode length. |
| **Stronger angle gains (Kθ = 18, Kθ̇ = 2.5)** | Provides a more aggressive torque when the pole tilts, but the scaling factor (max = 2) prevents the torque from becoming excessive. |
| **Non‑zero position‑only gains (Kx = 0.8, Kẋ = 0.1)** | Moves the cart back toward the centre faster while the pole is almost upright, reducing the chance that the cart drifts to the track edge and forces a large corrective torque later. |
| **Dead‑zone** | Eliminates unnecessary fighting of the pole when it is already balanced, letting the cart‑position controller dominate. |
| **Linear scaling (1 → 2)** | Guarantees a smooth transition from the dead‑zone to the safety‑stop, avoiding a sudden jump in force that could destabilise the system. |
| **Soft‑clipping with tanh** | The raw command is still limited to ±3 N, but the transition is smooth, which reduces jerky accelerations and helps keep the cart within the track limits. |
| **Finite‑check guard** | Prevents NaN/Inf from propagating into the controller (the same guard used in all previous policies). |

