| **All‑state feedback** | The cart‑position term is always present, so the cart is steered toward the centre *as soon as* the pole starts to tilt, preventing the cart from drifting to the edges. |
| **Higher angle gains (≈ 45, 10)** | These are comparable to the gains of a discretised LQR controller for the same system; they generate a strong enough torque to counteract the pole’s angular acceleration before it reaches the 0.02 rad “tiny‑band”. |
| **Early scaling (from 0.01 rad)** | The controller becomes more aggressive already when the pole is only a few hundredths of a radian away from vertical, which reduces the time spent in the “weak‑control” region that caused the pole to drift in the previous runs. |
| **Cap at 2.5×** | Guarantees the force never exceeds the physical limit (±3 N) after clipping, while still providing a noticeable boost when the pole is far from vertical. |
| **Emergency kick** | Keeps the safety net for the rare case that the pole still reaches the failure angle; the kick‑out is the same as before, so no new failure mode is introduced. |

