## Updated strategy (PD‑centric)

```
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Safety guard
if ( !isFinite(x)  or !isFinite(x_dot)
     or !isFinite(theta) or !isFinite(theta_dot) ) {
    force = 0.0
    return force
}

# 2. Hard‑stop when the pole is already out of the allowed band
if ( abs(theta) >= 0.20 ) {               # failure threshold
    force = -3.0 * sign(theta)            # push opposite to the tilt
    return force
}

# 3. PD controller on the pole angle
#    Gains were tuned empirically on the simulated cart‑pole.
Kp_angle   =  50.0      # proportional gain on θ   (rad⁻¹)
Kd_angle   =  10.0      # derivative gain on θ̇   (s)

# 4. Weak cart‑position controller (to keep the cart near zero)
Kp_cart    =  1.0       # proportional gain on x   (m⁻¹)
Kd_cart    =  0.5       # derivative gain on ẋ    (s)

# 5. Compute raw command
angle_term = -(Kp_angle * theta + Kd_angle * theta_dot)
cart_term  = -(Kp_cart  * x     + Kd_cart  * x_dot)

raw_force  = angle_term + cart_term

# 6. Optional dead‑zone (avoid constant micro‑twitching)
if ( abs(theta) < 0.01 and abs(theta_dot) < 0.02 and abs(x) < 0.02 )
    raw_force = 0.0

# 7. Saturate to the actuator limits
if ( raw_force >  3.0 ) force =  3.0
else if ( raw_force < -3.0 ) force = -3.0
else force = raw_force

return force
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
```

