| **Single smooth gain vector** | Removed the three‑zone scaling; the same K is used everywhere (except the hard‑stop). | No discontinuities → smoother trajectories, easier to tune, and less chance of “surprise” large forces. |
| **Hard‑stop threshold** | Slightly increased to |θ| ≥ 0.20 (instead of 0.18) and kept the max‑force action. | Gives the PD controller a little more room to recover before we resort to the brute‑force push. |
| **Higher pole gains** | `k_theta = 12`, `k_thetadot = 6` (≈ 1.5× larger than the best previous intermediate gain). | The raw command is usually well outside ±3 N when the pole is moderately tilted, so the clipping only occurs when the pole is truly close to failure. |

