| **Explicit cart‑bias (Kx, Kxdot)** – even in the intermediate zone we keep a small corrective term on the cart position/velocity. This prevents the cart from drifting to the edges of the track, which in turn keeps the pole’s dynamics more linear. |
| **Same emergency rule** – the hard‑stop at |θ| ≥ 0.18 rad is retained because it is essential for safety. |
| **Clipping after blending** – guarantees the command never exceeds the actuator limits, avoiding the “raw > 3 → 3” jumps that caused jerky behaviour in the first strategy. |
| **Finite‑state guard** – protects against NaNs / infinities that occasionally appear in simulation due to numerical overflow. |

