| 2    | 0.01 , 0.01 , ‑0.00 , 0.02 | 1.0 | 1.0 | ≈ ‑0.02 | ‑0.02 |
| …    | … | … | … | … | … |
| 18   | –0.01 , 0.19 , ‑0.03 , 0.79 | g_theta≈1.5 | g_cart≈0.6 | raw≈‑3.2 → clipped = ‑3.0 (hard‑push) | –3.0 |
| 19   | –0.03 , 0.27 , ‑1.03 , 3.15 | g_theta≈2.0 | g_cart≈0.3 | raw≈‑5.8 → clipped = ‑3.0 | –3.0 (still within limits) |

The new schedule would have **increased** the pole‑PD gain already at step 18 (g_theta ≈ 1.5 instead of the fixed 2.0 used previously) and **reduced** the cart term, so the controller would have applied a slightly larger corrective torque on the pole while not over‑driving the cart. This smoother transition should keep the pole from reaching the extreme angle (‑1.03 rad) that caused the failure.

