|-------------------------------------------|--------------------------|-----------------|-----------------------------|
| `[-0.01, 0.19, -0.03, 0.79]` (θ ≈ 0.19 rad) | `‑3 · sign(θ) = -3` (hard push left) | Cart slammed left, pole overshoots → failure | `scale ≈ (0.19‑0.02)/(0.20‑0.02) ≈ 0.94` → kθ≈23, kθd≈7.5 → raw ≈ ‑(23·0.19 + 7.5·0.79) ≈ ‑(4.37+5.93) ≈ ‑10.3 → clipped to ‑3, **but** the large kθd already damps the angular velocity, so the pole slows down before the cart reaches the edge. |
