|--------|--------------|-----------------|
| **Zone‑based gains** | Explicit “tiny / medium / large” split instead of a single linear interpolation from 0.02 → 0.18 rad. | The controller reacts earlier (at 0.10 rad) with a stronger bang‑bang component, preventing the pole from entering the runaway region. |
| **α‑blend** | In the medium zone the PD part is still present but its weight shrinks linearly with angle. | Gives a smooth hand‑over from gentle cart‑PD to aggressive bang‑bang, avoiding the abrupt “jump” that caused overshoot in the earlier attempts. |
| **Stronger θ̇ damping** | kθd grows from 1 → 7 (instead of 1 → 8) already at 0.10 rad, and is 8 in the large zone. | Damps the fast angular velocity that appears as the pole tips, reducing the overshoot that previously caused the crash around step ≈ 20. |
| **Cart‑PD in tiny zone** | Uses kx = 1, kxd = 0.5 (instead of the previous 1 · x + 0.5 · ẋ). | Keeps the cart centered without interfering with the pole when it is already very close to vertical. |
| **Bang‑bang always capped** | The bang component is limited to ±3 N before blending, so the final saturation step never “wastes” gain. | The controller uses the full available authority as soon as it is needed. |

