| **Rule 1 – “tilt‑raw”** (the very short rule set that only normalises the pole angle) | Use a single normalised “tilt” value and feed it directly to the force. | A simple monotonic mapping should keep the pole from drifting too far. | The pole still fell quickly; the force was far too small when the pole was near the limits and far too large when it was almost upright. | **45 / 1000** (the best single trial, but most runs were < 20) |
