| When `|θ|` falls below ~0.10 rad the boost disappears, leaving only the gentle linear term, which keeps the cart centred without fighting the pole unnecessarily. |

The controller therefore **pushes hard only when it is truly needed** and otherwise behaves like a well‑tuned linear regulator, which is exactly what the classic cart‑pole problem demands.

