| Component | What we changed | Expected effect |
|-----------|----------------|-----------------|
| **Dead‑zone** | 0.04 rad (slightly larger) | Stops the controller from reacting to noise while still giving early warning. |
| **Gain schedule** | Same quadratic shape as the 45‑point run, but **max Kp_pole = 32** and **max Kd_pole = 7** (the highest values we have already seen to work) | Guarantees enough torque when the pole is near the failure angle, preventing early saturation. |
| **Cart‑PD** | Same max values as before (0.40 / 0.10) – kept modest | Keeps the cart centred without creating large opposite swings. |
| **Feed‑forward** | Linear with tilt, magnitude up to 0.6 N, applied **before clipping** | Gives the cart a decisive nudge in the right direction exactly when the pole starts to fall fast, reducing the time the PD part spends at the force limit. |
| **Clipping order** | Clip only the final sum | The assist term is never lost to premature saturation. |

