| `Kd_theta` (increased from 0 → 7) | Damps angular velocity, stops the pole from “whipping” back and forth. |
| `Kp_cart` / `Kd_cart` (moderate values) | Keeps the cart near the centre, preventing it from hitting the track limits while not fighting the pole‑control. |
| `ff_gain` (up to 0.35) | Gives an early nudge in the direction of the tilt, reducing the peak `θ̇` that the PD terms must later cancel. |
| Linear interpolation on **all** gains | The controller is gentle when the pole is almost upright (low gains → low control noise) and becomes aggressive only when needed (high tilt). |
| `tanh` scaling | Guarantees the action stays inside `[-3, 3]` without hard clipping, which would otherwise introduce a discontinuity that can destabilise the PD loop. |

