| 8    | Using `sin(theta)` inside the PD term gives the correct torque direction while keeping the controller linear for tiny angles. |
| 9‑11 | A **tiny integral** on the pole angle removes the steady‑state offset that the pure PD left (only active when the pole is already close to vertical, otherwise it is reset). |
| 12‑13| Simple proportional centre‑bias (`‑0.12 x`) keeps the cart near the middle of the track. |
| 14‑15| Slightly stronger velocity damping (`‑0.04 ẋ`) damps the cart’s oscillations that appear when the pole pushes it. |
| 16‑18| `tanh` gives a smooth, bounded response; the final `clamp` guarantees we never exceed the actuator limits. |

