## Updated Strategy (the one we will adopt)

Below is a self‑contained pseudo‑code that can be copied directly into the simulation loop.  
All variables are assumed to be persisted between steps (`θ_int` is the integral of the pole angle).

```text
# --------------------------------------------------------------
#  CART‑POLE BALANCING CONTROLLER – version 4
# --------------------------------------------------------------
# Persistent state (initialised once at episode start)
θ_int ← 0.0                     # low‑pass integral of pole angle
last_force ← 0.0               # optional for smoothing (not used now)

# ----------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Safety check
# ----------------------------------------------------------------
IF NOT finite(x) OR NOT finite(x_dot) OR NOT finite(theta) OR NOT finite(theta_dot) THEN
    force ← 0.0
    RETURN force
END IF

# ----------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Normalised tilt (maps |θ|∈[0.05, 0.20] → [0,1])
#    Outside the interval we clamp to 0 or 1.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------
absθ ← ABS(theta)

IF absθ ≤ 0.05 THEN
    tilt_norm ← 0.0
ELSE IF absθ ≥ 0.20 THEN
    tilt_norm ← 1.0
ELSE
    tilt_norm ← (absθ - 0.05) / (0.20 - 0.05)   # linear mapping
END IF

# Use a *quadratic* scaling so that gains grow smoothly
gain ← tilt_norm * tilt_norm          # ∈[0,1]

# ----------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Gain scheduling for PD (and a tiny I term)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------
Kp  ← 4.0  + (14.0 - 4.0) * gain      # proportional gain  (4 → 14)
Kd  ← 2.5  + (9.0  - 2.5) * gain      # derivative gain    (2.5 → 9)
Ki  ← 0.02 * tilt_norm                # integral gain – very small

# ----------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Low‑pass integration of the pole angle
#    (leaky integrator to avoid wind‑up)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------
θ_int ← 0.99 * θ_int + 0.01 * theta    # 1 % new information each step

# ----------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Gravity feed‑forward (≈ actual torque)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------
gravity_ff ← 0.70 * 9.81 * SIN(theta)   # 0.70 ≈ tuned fraction of g·sinθ

# ----------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. PD‑I effort on the pole
# ----------------------------------------------------------------
pole_effort ← -(Kp * SIN(theta) + Kd * theta_dot + Ki * θ_int)

# ----------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. Cart‑centering effort (acts even when the pole is almost vertical)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------
cart_effort ← -(0.025 * x + 0.04 * x_dot)   # gentle spring‑damper on the cart

# ----------------------------------------------------------------
# 8. Optional small bias when the pole is very close to vertical
#    (helps to keep the cart centred without fighting the pole)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------
IF absθ < 0.07 THEN
    centre_bias ← -0.06 * x               # stronger than the 0.02 used before
ELSE
    centre_bias ← 0.0
END IF

# ----------------------------------------------------------------
# 9. Combine all contributions
# ----------------------------------------------------------------
raw_force ← pole_effort + gravity_ff + cart_effort + centre_bias

# ----------------------------------------------------------------
# 10. Saturate with a smooth tanh (keeps the force in [-3, 3] N)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------
force_raw ← 3.0 * TANH(0.30 * raw_force)

# ----------------------------------------------------------------
# 11. Final hard clip (just in case of numerical overflow)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------
IF force_raw > 3.0 THEN
    force ← 3.0
ELSE IF force_raw < -3.0 THEN
    force ← -3.0
ELSE
    force ← force_raw
END IF

RETURN force
```

