2. Compare the mean reward to the previous best (≈ 45 / 1000).  
3. If the mean exceeds ~ 70 / 1000, the added integral and stronger centre‑bias are paying off; otherwise, tune the coefficients (`Ki_theta`, `centre_bias` factor, or the gain ranges) in small increments.  

