Strategy C (the “best” one) is clearly the most effective.  Its simplicity, smooth gain‑schedule, modest gravity feed‑forward and weak centre‑bias together give a stable controller that can keep the pole upright for tens of seconds (≈ 45 % of a 100‑step episode on average).  The later, more complex strategies actually degraded performance.

