| **Tiny integral (`Ki ≤ 0.08`) + reset** | Removes steady‑state cart drift without building up a large wind‑up error when the pole swings widely. |
| **Gravity feed‑forward** | Cancels the dominant `g·sinθ` term, so the PD part only has to correct the *dynamic* error (θ̇, cart motion). |
| **Soft tanh saturation** | Guarantees a smooth transition to the force limits; the controller never experiences a hard “clamp” that would create a discontinuity in the dynamics. |
| **Dead‑zone = 0.01 N** | Eliminates high‑frequency jitter when the pole is perfectly balanced, yet is small enough not to starve the controller of needed torque. |
| **Light cart‑PD** | Keeps the cart from drifting to the track edges while not interfering with the pole‑stabilisation loop. |

