| Component | Reason it helps |
|-----------|-----------------|
| **Exponential tilt‑norm (`tilt_norm ** p`)** | Keeps the controller gentle when the pole is almost upright (preventing overshoot) but lets the gains explode as soon as the pole drifts past ~0.08 rad, giving the full 3 N when it is really needed. |
| **PD on the *raw* angle (`θ`)** | Directly penalises the actual deviation, eliminating the `sin(θ)`‑approximation error that slowed the earlier controllers. |
| **Integral on `θ` with Ki = 0.25** | Removes the small steady‑state bias that appears when the pole is held at a slight offset; the anti‑windup clamp prevents the integral from blowing up. |
| **Single tanh soft‑limit** | Uses the whole actuator range (‑3 … +3 N) while still providing a smooth transition that avoids a sudden “jump” when the command crosses zero. |
| **Dead‑zone of 0.01 N** | Stops the controller from constantly toggling around zero when the pole is perfectly balanced, which otherwise creates high‑frequency noise in the simulation. |

