**Bottom line:**  
The “tilt‑norm PD with gravity compensation, soft saturation and a tiny dead‑zone” is the most effective rule set we have discovered so far. Implement the pseudo‑code above, run a fresh batch of trials, and fine‑tune the gain limits if necessary. With this policy the pole should stay upright for many more timesteps than any of the previous attempts. Good luck!
