### 2️⃣ Updated rule‑set (the new “Balanced‑Pole” policy)

Below is a **self‑contained pseudo‑code** that can be copied straight into the environment’s decision function.  
All constants were chosen by hand after inspecting the reward history; they can be fine‑tuned later with a simple grid search.

```text
/* --------------------------------------------------------------
   Balanced‑Pole controller
   --------------------------------------------------------------
   Input  :  x, x_dot, theta, theta_dot   (float)
   Output :  force ∈ [‑3.0 , 3.0] (float)
   -------------------------------------------------------------- */

IF NOT ( isfinite(x) AND isfinite(x_dot) AND
         isfinite(theta) AND isfinite(theta_dot) ) THEN
    force ← 0.0
ELSE
    /* ----------------------------------------------------------
       1️⃣ Normalise the tilt (0 = perfectly vertical, 1 = “danger”)
       ---------------------------------------------------------- */
    tilt_abs      ← abs(theta)                     // |θ|
    /* we consider 0.02 rad as “already safe”, 0.20 rad as the
       absolute failure limit (the environment cuts off at 0.20). */
    tilt_norm_raw ← (tilt_abs - 0.02) / (0.20 - 0.02)

    IF tilt_norm_raw < 0.0 THEN
        tilt_norm ← 0.0
    ELSE IF tilt_norm_raw > 1.0 THEN
        tilt_norm ← 1.0
    ELSE
        tilt_norm ← tilt_norm_raw
    END IF

    /* ----------------------------------------------------------
       2️⃣ Gain‑scheduling (more aggressive when tilt_norm is high)
       ---------------------------------------------------------- */
    /* Safe (near‑vertical) gains */
    Kp_theta_safe ← 12.0      ; Kd_theta_safe ← 8.0
    Kp_x_safe     ← 0.4       ; Kd_x_safe     ← 0.4

    /* Aggressive (far‑from‑vertical) gains */
    Kp_theta_aggr ← 30.0      ; Kd_theta_aggr ← 20.0
    Kp_x_aggr     ← 1.2       ; Kd_x_aggr     ← 1.0

    /* Linear interpolation */
    Kp_theta ← (1.0 - tilt_norm) * Kp_theta_safe + tilt_norm * Kp_theta_aggr
    Kd_theta ← (1.0 - tilt_norm) * Kd_theta_safe + tilt_norm * Kd_theta_aggr
    Kp_x     ← (1.0 - tilt_norm) * Kp_x_safe     + tilt_norm * Kp_x_aggr
    Kd_x     ← (1.0 - tilt_norm) * Kd_x_safe     + tilt_norm * Kd_x_aggr

    /* ----------------------------------------------------------
       3️⃣ Emergency boost (starts earlier than the failure angle)
       ---------------------------------------------------------- */
    IF tilt_abs > 0.12 THEN                     // start boosting at 0.12 rad
        boost_factor ← (tilt_abs - 0.12) / (0.20 - 0.12)   // 0 … 1
        boost       ← 6.0 * boost_factor * sign(theta)   // max ±6 N
    ELSE
        boost ← 0.0
    END IF

    /* ----------------------------------------------------------
       4️⃣ Raw control law (PD on pole + PD on cart + boost)
       ---------------------------------------------------------- */
    u_raw ← -( Kp_theta * theta
               + Kd_theta * theta_dot
               + Kp_x     * x
               + Kd_x     * x_dot ) + boost

    /* ----------------------------------------------------------
       5️⃣ Gravity compensation (adds the component needed to hold
           the pole against gravity when the cart is still)
       ---------------------------------------------------------- */
    u_raw ← u_raw + 9.81 * sin(theta)

    /* ----------------------------------------------------------
       6️⃣ Map to admissible force (smooth saturation)
       ---------------------------------------------------------- */
    /* tanh gives a smooth transition; the divisor 2.0 controls
       how quickly we approach the ±3 N limit. */
    force_unclipped ← 3.0 * tanh( u_raw / 2.0 )

    /* Final clipping – protects against numerical overshoot */
    IF force_unclipped > 3.0 THEN
        force ← 3.0
    ELSE IF force_unclipped < -3.0 THEN
        force ← -3.0
    ELSE
        force ← force_unclipped
    END IF
END IF
```

