| Feature | Effect on performance |
|---------|-----------------------|
| **No hard dead‑zone (or a 0.02 N one)** | The controller can always apply the minute corrective pushes that keep the pole from drifting when it is almost upright. |
| **Soft gain‑blending (max 20 % high‑gain)** | Prevents the huge “kick” that previously sent the pole past ±0.2 rad, while still giving a little extra authority when the pole is far from vertical. |
| **Tiny integral term (Ki = 0.05, clamped)** | Cancels the slow bias caused by discretisation and the cart‑position offset, extending the balanced time without causing wind‑up. |
| **Small cart‑position gains (≈ 0.2 – 0.9)** | Keeps the cart from hitting the track ends, but does not dominate the pole‑stabilisation loop. |
| **tanh‑saturation with divisor = 1.0** | Gives a near‑linear response for the low‑force region (|u| < 1) and a smooth approach to the ±3 N limit, avoiding abrupt clipping that can destabilise the system. |
