[-0.01, 0.04, -0.33, 0.73]; -0.08   →  small negative force, pole still near centre
[-0.03, 0.07, -0.36, 0.80];  0.15   →  positive force, correcting the tilt
...
[0.29, -0.23, 1.15, -2.06]; None    →  pole about to exceed 0.2 rad, controller pushes hard
```

The pattern shows that the controller **reacts in the right direction** (force sign opposite to tilt) but **fails to generate enough magnitude** once the pole is > 0.15 rad.  The new `Fmax` growth (starting at 0.07 rad) and the stronger `Kd_theta` directly address this shortfall.

