|-----------|--------|
| **Quadratic tilt (`tilt = tilt_raw²`)** | Gives a gentle increase of gains for small tilts (avoids over‑reacting) while still reaching the maximum gain when the pole is close to the failure angle. |
| **Hard clipping only** | Allows the controller to use the full 3 N when a large corrective impulse is required (the main reason S3 out‑performed the other strategies). |
| **Very small cart‑position gains** | Keeps the cart near the centre, preventing it from hitting the track limits during aggressive pole corrections. |
| **Optional integral term** | Compensates for any tiny steady‑state bias that the PD alone cannot eliminate (e.g., due to model mismatch). The integral is bounded and reset when the pole is near vertical, so it never winds up. |
| **Safety guard on cart position** | Guarantees that a runaway cart is immediately driven back, which is useful when the pole is already falling and the controller tries to “push” the cart far away. |
| **Bias & gravity feed‑forward** | Both are retained because they have proven useful in all previous runs. |

### 4. Expected behaviour (qualitative)

