**4. Why this should work better**

| Component | Reason |
|-----------|--------|
| **Quadratic tilt scaling** | Gives a gentle response when the pole is almost upright (reduces chattering) and a strong response when the angle approaches the failure bound. |
| **Higher base gains (Kp = 30, Kd = 2)** | Guarantees enough torque even for small tilts; the extra gain added by `tilt` pushes the controller into the “catch‑up” regime before |θ| reaches 0.2 rad. |
| **Large gravity feed‑forward (0.9 sinθ)** | Offsets most of the pole’s own torque, so the PD part only needs to correct the *difference* between the actual and the desired torque. |
| **Cart‑centering term** | Prevents the cart from drifting to the track edges, which would otherwise cause early termination even if the pole is still upright. |
| **Clipping** | Guarantees the command stays within the physical limits; because the controller is already strong enough, clipping will rarely be active, keeping the dynamics linear. |

